For positive integer n, what is the tight running-time bound in the unit-cost arithmetic model, ignoring recursion limits?

```python
def power(x, n):
    if n == 0:
        return 1
    if n % 2 == 0:
        return (power(x, n // 2)
                * power(x, n // 2))
    return x * power(x, n - 1)
```
